    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now **deterministic** \u2014 the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` \u2014 so owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically, without any explicit linking step.\n\n**`HouseholdNormalizer`** (`util/HouseholdNormalizer.java`)\n- Replaced the address-based `householdKey`/`householdId(lastName, address)` pair with a single `householdId(lastName, postcode)` that hashes `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (last name trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/lower-cased; postcode used as-is, empty when absent). Dropped the old `HH-` prefix.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1`** (`addOwner` flow)\n- `applyHouseholdMembership` now: (1) always assigns the computed `householdId`; (2) treats any existing owner with the same `householdId` as the same household \u2014 a second such owner is rejected **409** as a household duplicate **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set, in which case it's created as a *declared household member*; (3) records `householdSize` (members + 1). It returns whether the owner is a declared member.\n- `sharesHousehold` now only **bypasses the duplicate block** \u2014 the linking/back-fill logic (`linkToHousehold`) is gone since the id is deterministic.\n- `sameHouseholdOwners` now matches by computed `householdId` instead of last-name+address.\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` skips flagging for a declared household member (\"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate\").\n- The existing identity-key check still runs after the household id is resolved, so it keys off the computed `householdId` (as `getIdentityKey()` already reads that field).\n\n**New exception** `HouseholdDuplicateException` (extends `OwnerConflictException` \u2192 maps to 409).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the now-stale `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions to match the new semantics.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nOne design note worth surfacing: I kept the pre-existing identity-key duplicate check in place alongside the new household-duplicate rule. Since `householdId` is now part of the identity key, an *exact* identity duplicate (same telephone + email + household) is still rejected 409 even with `sharesHousehold` set \u2014 `sharesHousehold` bypasses only the household block, not a fully-identical record. The spec's test doesn't exercise that case (owner `b` uses a distinct telephone), so this is a judgment call; let me know if you'd prefer `sharesHousehold` to bypass identity collisions too.",
